From a3c8236efabdd275d54f451c7fbf35618fb150b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 07:25:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10619/11171] Correct a false claim I repeated all night: the
 eval collects no supervisor receipts

scripts/arc_leaderboard_eval.py never calls trajectory_supervisor_diagnostics().
Its per-game rows carry no supervisor field. The only occurrence of the word
"supervisor" in that file is a comment I added earlier tonight, describing receipts
the script does not collect.

So the supervised run in flight since 2026-08-31 20:01Z cannot produce the evidence
it was started for, and could not have from the beginning. Setting
CARNOT_ARC_TRAJECTORY_SUPERVISOR=1 does make the supervisor APPLY its redirects, so
the agent's behaviour changes, but nothing serialises the firing counts and the
refinement ledger gains nothing.

I asserted the opposite in ops/status.md, in the REQ-ARC-WMTE-6850 rationale, in the
project_arc_eval_is_unobservable_until_it_ends memory, and in the commit messages of
dac8043123, ae229ac429 and b83c0f2402 -- each saying a death would lose "every
trajectory-supervisor receipt they had accrued". There are none to lose. The
correction is appended to ops/status.md rather than replacing the original text, and
it lists every place the claim was repeated so a reader can discount all of it.

Worth separating from the error: the run is producing real adapter-free level data.
ls20 finished live=L0 (+0), 2443 actions, efficiency 0.0000, in 26,340s -- a genuine
null for the frame-only path on that game, and the reason the operator chose to let
wa30 finish rather than kill the run.

The harness that does collect receipts is scripts/arc_scored_path_lever_harness.py.
It emits the field on every row on both paths and turns a raising diagnostics call
into an error marker rather than dropping the field; its own comment records that an
absent field reading as zero cost a full day of wrong A/B reporting on 2026-08-21. A
launcher now waits for GPU 1 to free, then runs that harness applied on m0r0 and
sk48 -- both zero-level games, because redirects fire on stagnation and zero-level
games buy firings most cheaply, which was the original ls20/wa30 reasoning.

Also recorded: when wa30 started at 07:20Z the generator guard found 963 MiB free on
GPU 1 and warned it would decline the card and fall back to the iGPU. No second
server was spawned -- one llama-server exists and serves at ~27 tok/s -- so wa30 runs
on the existing server. The warning describes what would have happened to a new
generator, not what happened.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
